comments:
Having a getSize counterpart to setSize seems pretty different from #19733. getSize() is very useful when trying to make the container responsive. Take a look at https://codepen.io/scscscsc/pen/zYrwxBj . The getFrustrum() function has the following:
```javascript
	var renderSize;
	if(useSVGRenderer) {
		var containerBox = container.getBoundingClientRect();
		renderSize = new THREE.Vector2(containerBox.width, containerBox.height);
	} else {
		renderSize = renderer.getSize(new THREE.Vector2());
	}
```

I'd much rather call renderer.getSize(), which is just stuffing two internal variables in to a Vector2, whereas getBoundingClientRect() is slow and I generally try to avoid it.

